{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773168687,"nonce":"JiMWv72XrAfus+0ePGK9bwnTMLo=","title":"Reviewer agent: auto-review agent work before human review","message":"Implement an automated reviewer agent that reviews the coding agent's work when it reaches `waiting:review` status, before involving the human.\n\n## Flow\n\n1. Coder agent finishes → status becomes `waiting:review`\n2. Watcher detects `waiting:review` and triggers the reviewer agent\n3. Reviewer reads the git diff (base_branch..agent branch), runs tests if configured, and evaluates the work\n4. Reviewer posts structured feedback as a tracker comment:\n   - If satisfied: posts `@nightshift accept` (or a new `@nightshift approve` that signals human can do final review)\n   - If not satisfied: posts `@nightshift revise` with specific feedback\n5. Coder resumes with feedback, loop continues\n\n## Design Considerations\n\n- Reviewer should be lightweight — no Docker container needed, just reads diff and calls an LLM\n- Could be a new adapter type (e.g. `reviewer` in WORKFLOW.md config)\n- Or a watcher-integrated step that runs before notifying the human\n- Should be configurable: enable/disable, max review rounds, auto-accept threshold\n- Reviewer should not auto-accept by default — instead post a summary for human to confirm\n- Consider a `@nightshift approve` command that means \"reviewer is satisfied, awaiting human confirmation\" vs `@nightshift accept` which means \"merge now\"\n\n## Future Extension\n\n- Intake/clarification agent that runs before the coder to ensure issue clarity","files":null}]}